From 4178f6f741afee08a539a044e7775b5ea0d26e62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: askimi <44218719+RNI4114@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 16:53:45 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] anv/xe: resolve queue-to-queue timeline waits without
 the kernel (experimental)

Same-queue waits on values already signaled by an earlier submission of the
same queue are dropped (jobs of one exec queue run in order). Waits of the
compute queue on hot semaphores signaled by another queue poll a memory slot
with MI_SEMAPHORE_WAIT; signaling submissions publish the value from a tail
batch the last command buffer jumps to. Render queue waits stay kernel
dependencies: an active render context makes the compute engine ~2.5x slower
on BMG. ANV_XQ=0 disables, ANV_XQ_SAME/ANV_XQ_CROSS/ANV_XQ_ONLY/ANV_XQ_LIGHT/
ANV_XQ_SMEM/ANV_XQ_STATS for experiments. Test: rt-profiling/morta/xqtest.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit c367195b1a5a2c45f042bcf4f5dbef661e603734)
(cherry picked from commit 8f364e41056552027294bdb20a32ed8d2246630c)
